    "vintage": "2024",
    "retrieved": "2026-11-01",
    "crs": "NAD83 longitude/latitude (EPSG:4269), as published",
    "bboxMethod": "GDAL/OGR envelope of each county polygon, rounded outward to 6 decimal places. The 1:500,000 file is generalized, so a bbox can differ from full-resolution TIGER/Line by a few hundred meters."
  },
  "selection": "For each state FIPS code in the file, the county with the lowest GEOID among counties whose bbox overlaps the CCRS coarse envelope (lon -124.6 to -114.0, lat 32.4 to 42.1); where no county overlaps it, the lowest GEOID in the state. This puts a county inside the California rectangle in every state where one exists (AZ, CA, ID, NV, OR, UT).",
  "expectationBasis": "Written from each registry's declared coverage, not from running the code: CCRS declares state 06 only; the ODOT crash-layer adapter declares state 41 only and is read-only (not admitted to safety_crashes), so Oregon reads it live while an Oregon acquisition still stores FARS; the FARS adapter reads NHTSA's National annual file, which carries the 50 states and DC (51 STATE values in the 2023 file), and, since 2026-11-02, NHTSA's separate Puerto Rico annual file (STATE 43, mapped to FIPS 72); the VMT significance framework registry declares US-CA only; grant program state bundles declare US-CA, US-WA, US-OR, US-CO, US-TX and US-OH. null means none registered.",
